/-- **ν and an optimal pose of `Johnson.Bilunabirotunda.polyhedron` as one root**: when the representatives' systems have
exactly one root each, of scale `N`, the system `S` has exactly one root, of scale `N`, and at it
`matAt x 45`, `matAt x 36` and `(x 54, x 55)` are a weak fit of `Johnson.Bilunabirotunda.polyhedron` scaled
by `N` through itself. -/
theorem johnsonBilunabirotunda_pose_of_reps {N : ℝ} (h : PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq [Pose.JohnsonBilunabirotunda.reps0] N) :
    PolynomialSystem.IsPoseRoot Johnson.Bilunabirotunda.polyhedron Pose.JohnsonBilunabirotunda.S N 45 36 54 := by
  rw [Pose.JohnsonBilunabirotunda.S_eq]
  exact PolynomialSystem.ct_isPoseRoot h List.mem_cons_self Pose.JohnsonBilunabirotunda.len_eq Pose.JohnsonBilunabirotunda.reps_eq
    (Root.ParData.sqrt_spec (by decide +kernel)) Pose.JohnsonBilunabirotunda.par_ok Pose.JohnsonBilunabirotunda.zs_eq Pose.JohnsonBilunabirotunda.weak_ok Pose.JohnsonBilunabirotunda.poly_eq Pose.JohnsonBilunabirotunda.ok

end Nieuwland.Polyhedra
